        "\n",
        "# Focus of Today\n",
        "\n",
        "<br> <br>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.value-box fragment=\"fade-in\" value=\"NOT trying to teach you everything about location optimization\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.value-box fragment=\"fade-in\" value=\"Telling you about this package so you can feed into its development\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "# What is location optimization?\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "##\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment}\n",
        "\n",
        "Where should I put my healthcare resources?\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.focus-list}\n",
        "- If I'm closing one service, which should it be?\n",
        "- If I'm adding a new site to an existing service, which of these 5 possible places should I put it?\n",
        "- If I'm spinning up a totally new service, how should I distribute my sites?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# The Current (Python) Landscape\n",
        "\n",
        "## [spopt](https://pysal.org/spopt/)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "### Pros\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.focus-list}\n",
        "- Part of a wider ecosystem ([pysal](https://pysal.org/) - **P**ython **S**patial **A**nalysis **L**ibrary)\n",
        "- 350+ github stars\n",
        "- 24 contributors (i.e. pretty robust)\n",
        "- Quite a lot of documentation...\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.focus-list}\n",
        "- ... but the documentation is (imo) quite confusing\n",
        "- Not healthcare or UK focussed\n",
        "- Linear optimization returns a single option by default\n",
        "- Need to manually create your own output plots\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## [HSMA](https://hsma.co.uk/hsma_content/modules/current_module_details/3_geographic_modelling_visualisation.html) and [Open Source Exeter MSc content](https://github.com/health-data-science-OR/healthcare-logistics/tree/master/optimisation)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "### Pros\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.focus-list}\n",
        "- Returns multiple options\n",
        "- Written with UK healthcare in mind\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "\n",
        "### Cons\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.focus-list}\n",
        "- Requires manual copying and adapting of code\n",
        "- Still need to manually create your own plots\n",
        "- Risk of more errors due to unreviewed code without automated tests\n",
        "- Still lots of repetition across organisations\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## lokigi\n",
        "\n",
        "Lokigi is a brand new package building on the HSMA and Exeter approach.\n",
        "\n",
        "It aims to provide an easy-to-use workflow to simplify and speed up location optimization work.\n",
        "\n",
        "## lokigi\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "<center>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.value-box align=\"center\" style=\"font-size: 2.75rem;\" value=\"The goal is to make it work optimally for <br> **UK healthcare contexts**\"}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment}\n",
        "If it works for other contexts, it's a bonus - not the other way around.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "</center>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Simple Problem Formulation\n",
        "\n",
        "At its core, you only need a travel matrix."
      ],
      "id": "ff6bf4de"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hsma-tools/lokigi/refs/heads/main/sample_data/devon_miu_travel_matrix.csv\")\n",
        "from IPython.display import HTML\n",
        "HTML(df.head(3)[[\"from_id\",\"Cumberland Centre (Plymouth)\", \"Dawlish Community Hospital\", \"Derriford Hospital (UTC)\", \"Exmouth Minor Injury Unit\"]].to_html(classes=\"styled-table\", index=False))"
      ],
      "id": "3c7b62b7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Setting up your problem is easy.\n"
      ],
      "id": "156897bd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "from lokigi.site import SiteProblem\n",
        "\n",
        "problem = SiteProblem()\n",
        "\n",
        "problem.add_travel_matrix(\n",
        "    travel_matrix_df=\"path/to/devon_miu_travel_matrix.csv\",\n",
        "    source_col=\"from_id\",\n",
        "    unit=\"minutes\",\n",
        "    )"
      ],
      "id": "af334b28",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "from lokigi.site import SiteProblem\n",
        "\n",
        "problem = SiteProblem()\n",
        "\n",
        "problem.add_travel_matrix(\n",
        "    travel_matrix_df=\"https://github.com/hsma-tools/lokigi/blob/main/sample_data/devon_miu_travel_matrix.csv\",\n",
        "    source_col=\"from_id\",\n",
        "    unit=\"minutes\",\n",
        "    )"
      ],
      "id": "44b25119",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "<br/>\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment}\n",
        "\n",
        "And you can solve it with a single command."
      ],
      "id": "83cea10b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "solution = problem.solve(p=4)"
      ],
      "id": "f9d78247",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "(as it assumes the columns in your travel matrix = your potential sites)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.fragment .fade-in-then-semi-out}\n",
        "By default, lokigi will\n",
        "\n",
        "- brute force the solution\n",
        "- assume you want to solve a p-median problem [(minimize travel time - weighted by demand if you provide that)]{style=\"color:DarkGrey;\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment .fade-in-then-semi-out}\n",
        "It also supports\n",
        "\n",
        "- p-center [(minimizing max travel time)]{style=\"color:DarkGrey;\"}\n",
        "- the Maximal Covering Location Problem [(given x sites, how to we maximise people within y distance?)]{style=\"color:DarkGrey;\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "You can then see a range of metrics for all possible solutions."
      ],
      "id": "0d92e6f0"
